Thinking Machines Lab gives 32GB as the minimum RAM requirement for Inkling 2 Mini on Mac, but with the Q3 quant I felt it must be possible to get somewhere reasonable on my 24GB M2 MacBook Air. Llama.cpp wasn&#x27;t cutting it even with patches, so I spent this week&#x27;s Fable allowance (with a sprinkling of Astra) on this custom inference engine, and took the opportunity to add some optimisations and ergonomics for running on a memory-constrained laptop: - strictly one model loaded at a time, requests queued;
- KV cache gets saved and model unloaded after every response (or configurable delay), so RAM stays at 50MB between calls, but reload is fast;
